WEBVTT

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:06.780
Our first summer of high school is over.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.980
I feel like it went by much more quickly than usual.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.690
You too? I was just thinking the same thing.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:16.770
That's just proof of how much fun it was.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.410
It slipped away too fast.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:23.660
Yeah, if only time crawled when you were having fun. {## this one isn't just pedantry, people actually do not make this mistake (cf. kinda pedantic 'if it were'), since they'll get the tense right and 'were' is the past of second person 'be' (cf. 'if it were''s weird shift from typical 'was' to 'were')}{have you MET people? ever?}

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.050
But we really did get to do so many different things.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.030
I wonder how autumn will turn out. {## Fowler apparently prefers that people use 'autumn', but regrets that that's the case because he thinks 'Fall' is just better (but an Americanism). got a feeling so complicated}

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:45.060
They call it the evening of the year, 
and the days start getting shorter too. {## or 'that season', since she's talking about it from a distance. 'this' would forbid her speaking of 'how autumn will turn out' / the second half is to avoid a weird and undesirable evening/sunset parallel / the whole sentence doesn't seem like it follows in the English, but there doesn't appear to be much to be done}

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:49.650
Teko-san, Teko-san. We're gonna have a problem if you underestimate autumn's true power.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:53.450
Autumn is chock-full of bountiful fun to be had too! {she doubles too}{## preferably uncountable / mass noun for 'bountiful', alt. 'bountifully fun activities' but the meaning shifts}

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:57.490
Just look around and you'll find yourself surrounded by autumn wonders! {## apart from being cool and literal, suppots the next line. it's weird to talk about a single wonder, and then talk about -another- single wonder coming by; this type of plural -> singular structure here is more common}

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:02.450
Freshly roasted sweet potatoes... {## I almost played myself, but there is indeed no hyphen}

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.720
And speak of the devil, one's heading our way now!

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.850
Roasted sweet potatoes! {## I don't care what the Japanese call it, you can't refer to sweet potatoes as 'potatoes'. if you want it shorter, just 'Sweet potatoes!'}

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.920
Oh no, oh no! Oh no! {## can you retime this so it starts fully after the 'aah' at the start?}

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.860
Hot! That's hot, hot, hot! {## there are three of them and 'that' doesn't count as a word / OLE OLE OLE OLE FEELING HOT HOT HOT}

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:22.100
Oh no, oh no, oh no, oh no...

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:29.570
Let's eat!

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.510
You were right. I should respect autumn. {## first Yuru Camp hotpot and now this, my imaginary mouth can't take it}

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.760
Right, right? I told you!

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.290
Pikari!

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.530
Are you okay?

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:03.100
If I let something like this get me down, 
I'll never conquer all of autumn's wonders!

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.920
I see, so autumn is a tough foe!

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:15.260
There's so much I wanted to talk to you about

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:15.260
hanashitakatta koto takusan atta no ni

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:20.600
But my mind went blank when I saw your face

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:20.600
kao miru to wasurechau

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:29.210
Every time you peek in to pick me up after school my heart lights up

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:29.210
houkago mukae ni kitekureru no ga ureshikute

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:36.460
I wonder why I so hopelessly feel this way about you

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:36.460
doushite kimi ja nakucha dame na no kana

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:41.950
It can't be explained with words

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:41.950
setsumei wa dekinai no

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:50.210
Maybe it's like how we can't live without the sun or sea

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:50.210
taiyou ya mizu ga hitsuyou na no to niteru ki ga suru

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:50.210
Maybe it's like how we can't live without the sun or sea

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:50.210
taiyou ya mizu ga hitsuyou na no to niteru ki ga suru

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:57.600
The days have begun to get shorter now

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:57.600
hi ga mijikaku nattekita ne

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:05.730
Why must they cut off my time with you?

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:05.730
mou chotto issho ni itai no ni

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:11.340
Tomorrow and the day after, and every day forevermore

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:11.340
ashita mo asatte mo sono saki mo zutto

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:16.490
I want to keep walking home together like this

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:16.490
kouyatte kimi to kaeritai

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:21.940
No matter what the weather was, no matter how my day went

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:21.940
donna tenki demo donna kibun demo

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:29.710
The moment you raise your hand to wave goodbye

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:29.710
mata ne to kimi ga te wo furu toki

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:37.690
I feel like it has been a wonderful day

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:37.690
ii hi datta to omoeru kara

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.550
Huh?

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:07.220
It's her.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:09.740
Pi—

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.690
Whoa, that was close. I almost raised my voice just now. {## 'almost just' is a weird}{no it's not}

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:19.450
I'd only embarrass myself if I yelled across the street like that.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:25.090
Kokoro-chan!

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:27.500
It's me! Do you remember? {## charlotte.png}

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.290
Pikari...san.

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:30.610
Ding-dong! {## is this possible better off as 'bingo' or something or is she just baka}

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.510
Whew, talk about coincidence! Are you by yourself? {## wew / total pref. to my ear 'alone' sounds both more formal and more... threatening? dunno}

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:35.710
Yes, my parents asked me to shop for—

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.460
Stop!

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.900
Let me guess! Your target is...

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:44.510
That, right? {## long enough gap, and strong stress}

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:48.430
The autumn-exclusive chestnut pie! {the only other option is Boulette Au Marron}{## why boulette (balls)? 'tarte aux marrons', more likely? but anyway let's avoid frog if we can / I guess just 'autumn' all the time}

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:52.620
I knew it! I've been looking forward to it too.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:55.070
Like I said, I'm not here for me, but for my paren— {## further, referring to 'it' means the pie, but Kokoro's talking about her shopping trip in general ('i'm not even here for myself, so don't drag me off for some pie that isn't even related to what I'm here for') / side note putting the break after 'parent' makes it look like a singular, should be 'paren' if you want to cut it off mid-word}

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:57.060
Great minds think alike! Let's get in line!

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:05.700
<i>Autumn wonders.</i>

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.000
<i>For example...</i>

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:10.400
<i>Time spent like this.</i>

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.590
<i>Bathing in gentle, relaxing sunlight,</i>

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:21.300
<i>leisurely enjoying my favorite book at a terrace café. {## the PRIDE OF ENGLISH / not raised, not a terrace, and a terrace cafe (probably 'terraced cafe', even) =/= a cafe's terrace}</i>

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:26.960
<i>My reading companions, a sweet potato and a pumpkin latte. {## similar structure to prev / otherwise sweet-potato-and-pumpkin latte / PUMPKIN SPICE LATTE}</i>

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:30.220
Where should we head next?

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.970
This says we're near Sakura Village. {back in s1 I used cherry blossom, but here it's more useful to use sakura}{## particle unnecessary, probably; I -think- near is preferable here, while nearby is preferable when there's no object? pref}

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:34.870
Sakura Village?

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:37.590
What's the point in going there during fall?

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:39.440
Apparently they bloom in this season too. {## ostensibly the same ones that bloomed in spring, and without 'too' sounds exclusive one season only}

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.510
They're called October sakura.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:41.940
Really?

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:44.400
But shouldn't we go in the spring? {## there's no reason to pull 'might as well', that needs supporting evidence to use (like if it's already almost over for the fall, or something)}

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.750
They're definitely better then. {## why not both, dude?}

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.190
You think so?

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.630
<i>We match.</i>

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:06.840
I missed my chance to try these autumn-only chestnut pies last year, so I'm definitely getting them this time. {## not consistent but totally fine / 'looking forward to them [ever since I didn't have one]' it's weird (among other reasons, she was looking forward to it last year too). why not just the Japanese?}

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.480
Kokoro-chan, we haven't seen each other since that time in the ocean.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:11.820
Have you been well?

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.810
Yeah, I guess.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:20.110
We must have a lot in common, running into each other like this both on land and in the sea. {## 'on ... sea' is no, I know this is clunky}

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:20.770
Sure.

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:32.870
The autumn wind feels so nice.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.830
It makes me miss summer. {## I guess I will give up this easily this time}

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:43.550
Kokoro-chan! Rock, paper, scissors!

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.840
Lose if you look... there! {## wat}

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:53.290
You finally raised your eyes.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:58.690
You'll miss all the autumn wonders if you're always looking down.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:00.040
Autumn wonders?

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:00.650
Yep!

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:04.150
The sky is so high.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:08.110
It really feels great.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.500
<i>This feels nice. {## reasons. 'this' is better with no prior setup than 'it', so these two were reversed}</i>

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:27.710
<i>That girl...</i>

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:30.590
<i>Her bag will fall off her lap. {## it's all premonitory, like the next two}</i>

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:42.140
<i>That cat is about to topple over.</i>

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.910
<i>The next person who leaves the shop...</i>

00:07:54.380 --> 00:08:00.080
<i>Yes, it'll be a mature lady with long, 
blonde hair, stylish sunglasses, and a nice body. {## I had to give 'sunglasses' an adjective since both 'hair' and 'body' had them}</i>

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:06.250
<i>I get it now.</i>

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.330
<i>This must be a dream. {## man did you learn nothing from the last episode}</i>

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:12.010
<i>In that case... {## flying witch s2 when}</i>

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.780
<i>See? It's just like I thought.</i>

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:11.100
Um, excuse me.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:15.820
Were you flying just now?

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:19.030
Yes, because this is a dream.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:37.500
They look so comfortable sleeping like that.

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:40.350
Towano-sensei, you're working this weekend too? {## man do I ever hate eye block haircut guys like this}

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:43.640
Yeah, what with midterms coming up soon.

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.470
Could I interest you in one of these? {## yes, mans -can- offer}

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:50.700
An autumn-exclusive mushroom bun? {## 'isn't that' doesn't well fit this context in English}

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:51.720
Are you sure?

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:54.270
Please, take it. They're really delicious.

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.990
Then I'll gladly accept.

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:59.340
Now if only we had beer, it'd be perfect.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:01.450
Agreed. {## 'count me in' is for actual real plans, doesn't make sense for a) hypotheticals and b) opinions}

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:06.160
Cats have got it made, being able to sleep the whole day away. {## 'got the life' ounds all sort of weird to me}

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:08.670
You think they're sleeping in their dreams too?

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:10.810
Maybe they're drinking beer.

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:12.250
Oh, please!

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:15.590
I see.

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.550
So it's a dream.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:20.300
No wonder. {## y-yohane?}

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:25.470
I had the vague impression it had to be, but I wasn't sure.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:30.880
This might be the first time I've ever realized that while still dreaming. {## because 'was' sort of wraps a number of possible past tenses here, reworked to be more specific / you could also just use 'lucid'}

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:32.240
It's a lot of fun.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:32.940
Huh?

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.150
Believe it or not, I'm a professional dreamer. {## 'dreaming pro' for 'consistency' with earlier instances of happiness pro, but}

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:42.270
Shall I teach you how to fly?

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:44.580
Huh? Y-Yes, please.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:50.500
First we'll need a broom for me, and a broom for you.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.910
Huh? But there's only one here.

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:55.460
Just imagine it.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.340
Imagine?

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.380
I'll use this one.

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:05.100
A bamboo broom... Very traditional. {## 'it's very traditional': this particular bamboo broom is very traditional. 'very traditional' attaches to something else, and we have: brooms made of bamboo are very traditional. effectively there's a ghost 'That's' instead of 'It's' and then we have normal that/it fuckery}

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:09.060
If you'd prefer something else, 
try visualizing one more your style.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:12.690
More my style? {## repetition like this is usually exact, and usually the end}

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:17.480
How cute! You're very good. {## 'doing great'}

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:21.770
Can I really ride this?

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:23.740
You don't ride the broom. {## orig. 'that broom's not for riding, [it's for sweeping]'. implies that that -specific- broom is not what will be used, but Teko means brooms in general}

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:25.080
You don't?

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:28.280
In a dream, all you need is imagination.

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:32.570
The broom is just a tool to help you imagine yourself flying.

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:35.040
Go on, give it a try.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.230
Okay.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.490
Imagine myself flying.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:50.680
Um, it doesn't look like I can do it.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:52.140
Sure you can.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:53.790
Let's fly together.

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:55.180
Together?

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:01.810
Point the tip of your broom upwards and you'll start to float.

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:02.570
Okay.

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:04.200
Here we go.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.140
Okay.

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:06.660
One, and...

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.650
Go!

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:20.290
You did it!

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:21.880
It worked!

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:26.720
Point your broom left when you want to go that way, and point it right when you want to go the other.

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:31.460
The broom is just for sitting on. 
You're the one who's actually flying.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:32.850
Right!

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:44.150
I can't stop!

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.990
Open your eyes.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:47.720
I can't, I can't, I can't, I can't!

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:50.310
You'll be fine. I'm right here with you.

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:01.090
Wow!

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:05.050
I feel like I'm a witch!

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:09.010
Real witches need familiars, don't you think? {no, I'm saying that they're not real unless they have familiars}

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:14.440
So adorable!

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:25.070
Isn't this fun?

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:29.450
You can do anything you want once you realize you're in a dream.

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:37.790
In real life, I'm so shy that I get scared in front of strangers and have a hard time talking to them.

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:40.610
What? Is that true?

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.580
You don't seem that way at all.

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:50.760
I bet Pikari would be surprised if she saw me acting like this.

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:55.480
Time to dig in!

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:02.240
Isn't it yummy, Kokoro-chan? {## that isn't a goddamn pie. a crepe with balls...? what am I looking at}

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:06.650
Doesn't eating one of autumn's wonders make you feel all warm inside?

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:18.710
To be honest, something kind of bad happened to me at school.

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.300
It's been bothering me. {## kids don't say 'weighing'. -i- don't even say weighing}

00:14:22.530 --> 00:14:24.380
What happened?

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:28.630
Someone scribbled... in my notebook.

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:31.450
They called me octo-lips. {## where does that depiction of an octopus even come from? octopuses don't have mouths like that, who thought of that?}{are you sure you watch anime}

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:34.970
They even drew a cute picture. {## well, then it's fine then isn't it}

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:39.300
Just laugh if you want to!

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:49.370
I don't understand it one bit. 
What's so fun about teasing other people?

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:54.790
I see, so that's what was making you feel bad.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:15:00.290
People who do unmanly things like that are the absolute worst. {## the original was just overall weird, especially 'no matter what anyone else says', when no one else had said anything. forgive my cool literal rewrite}

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:08.050
Maybe the boy who did it actually likes you! {## remind me, is kokoro a girl or a boy}{you figure it out}

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:11.650
Huh?! That makes even less sense! {## looked at making this match, but it was awkward}

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:13.090
I'd only hate them more!

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:14.010
Whoopsie.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:19.120
Don't you get angry when you don't know the reason someone did something stupid? {## match below}

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:21.000
The reason, huh.

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:24.210
What's the harm in not knowing?

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:25.060
Huh?

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:28.690
Trying to understand it would just make you feel even worse.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:31.280
No, I won't ever be satisfied like that.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:33.790
I'm gonna find out who did it.

00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:37.240
What'll you do then?

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.790
Punch his lights out!

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:45.740
Kokoro-chan, you'll definitely regret it if you do.

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:46.590
Huh?

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:47.920
Let's go.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:49.050
What?

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:51.380
Go where?

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:54.300
Where are we going?

00:15:56.800 --> 00:16:00.730
Since we're up here, I figured we could go searching for autumn's wonders.

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:02.590
Autumn's wonders?

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:04.970
For example...

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.650
Have you heard of Sakura Village? {## ah, and now no 'the'}

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:10.550
On Mount Oomuro? {## sakurako best girl}

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:12.700
Yes, I've been there a few times.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:15.200
Really? Then lead the way! {## can't lead yourself, so this'd be 'lead me' because there is no 'us' because can't lead yourself. but this, instead}

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:17.910
I want to see sakura that bloom in fall!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.040
Are you talking about October sakura?

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:22.920
I went to see them with my family before, but... {## ugh, reasons}

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:25.750
Okay! Now then, let's-a go! {## i -will- pick a fight over this if I have to. if you want this changed ping me and we'll talk about it}

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:28.380
What?! Wait, but...

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:32.400
Yay, I'm on a date with Kokoro-chan!

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:44.690
This is the right place...

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:48.900
But we couldn't find any, even after searching all around.

